{
  "_comment": "Spawn pools for the \"Count Roll (labs)\" variant - same shape/engine as enemies.mode2.data.json, but Monolith/UNISG/Sin are available at every tier (not Expert-only) since they can show up in lab encounters regardless of preset. Tier-first: category -> tier -> group -> { sections, count, min, max, icon }. A single-group reward (rolls=1) picks ONE random group from the tier and spawns exactly `count` creatures. A multi-group reward (rolls>1, e.g. 'x3') picks that many groups (independently - the same group can come up more than once) and spawns a RANDOM count for each, in [min, max] - default (no min/max set) is [max(1,count-1), count], so it just works without touching this file; set min/max on a specific group to hand-tune it (min=max=1 pins a boss-type group to always roll exactly 1 even in a x3 draw). Each creature is a random pick from that group's `sections`. `label` overrides the group key shown on the overlay / in the in-game message. `icon` is a public/ path for the overlay reel (mutant-icons/, patch-icons/); omitted where no icon exists yet. Mutant sections verified against this GAMMA install's actual creature configs (temp/mutant-sections-full.txt). Weak/normal/strong (and similar) naming variants have no actual gameplay difference, so each mutant species uses the SAME unified `sections` pool across every tier it appears in - only `count`/`min`/`max` scale with tier, not which section names are reachable. Edit freely - unknown sections are skipped by the Lua side.",
